Vita: J3D's shape display lists and vertex-format lists by reference, and the arrays they load
(port of the 3DS port's dusklight patches 0020 and 0023; with patches/aurora/0006).

J3DShapeDraw::draw and J3DShape's vertex-format list (mVcdVatCmd) go to the GX with
GXCallDisplayListStatic. Every place that changes such a list's bytes after it was made calls
GXInvalidateDisplayListStatic (J3DShapeDraw's list copies, addTexMtxIndexInDL, J3DSkinDeform's
in-place removal of matrix indices, makeVcdVatCmd). The arrays those lists load are the model's
own; J3D changes them in place only after a J3DVertexBuffer swap, so every swap names both of its
arrays to GXInvalidateArrayStatic. Same commands to the GX; no game logic changes. With the
backend's mode off, GXCallDisplayListStatic is GXCallDisplayList.

